Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:46:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(resource-packs): inherit client entity descriptions
 across layers

Resolve each client entity by identifier across the ordered pack stack. Merge alias dictionaries and script fields before parsing converter data, so a higher layer can override one alias or its scale without discarding lower animation roots. Return independent raw description snapshots for fields outside the converter model.

Live probes of Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 confirm that a higher scale overrides the lower scale, omitted animate roots survive, and overriding the right-arm alias retains the lower left-arm alias and its pose. Arrays and scalar values replace their lower values. Parsed data and raw snapshots publish together after validation.

Expose the same immutable description merger for licensed appearance readers. This keeps server and account graphs on one core inheritance algorithm while the add-on bridges its separate Gson types. Test nested list and object ownership at the public boundary.
